G5600.b:
⟪εἰμί⟫, with various uses and significations, like the English verb ⟪to be⟫.
⟪I.⟫ As substantive verb.
	⟪1.⟫ Of persons and things, ⟪to be, exist⟫: ⟦Acts 17:28|Ac 17:28⟧, ⟦John 1:1|Jo 1:1⟧ ⟦John 8:58|8:58⟧ ⟦John 17:5|17:5⟧, al; ὁ ὢν καὶ ὁ ἦν (for past ptcp.), ⟦Revelation 1:4|Re 1:4⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:8|8⟧ ⟦Revelation 4:8|4:8⟧ ⟦Revelation 11:17|11:17⟧ ⟦Revelation 16:5|16:5⟧ (v. Swete, Ap., 5; M, Pr., 228); τὰ (μὴ) ὄντα, ⟦Romans 4:17|Ro 4:17⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:28|I Co 1:28⟧.
	⟪2.⟫ Of times, events, etc., ⟪to be, happen, take place⟫: ⟦Matthew 24:3|Mt 24:3⟧, ⟦Mark 14:2|Mk 14:2⟧ ⟦Mark 15:42|15:42⟧, ⟦Luke 21:23|Lk 21:23⟧, ⟦John 4:6|Jo 4:6⟧, ⟦John 4:23|23⟧ ⟦John 5:10|5:10⟧, al.
	⟪3.⟫ ⟪to be present, be⟫ in a place, ⟪have come⟫: ⟦Matthew 2:13|Mt 2:13⟧, ⟦Matthew 2:15|15⟧, ⟦Mark 1:45|Mk 1:45⟧ ⟦Mark 5:21|5:21⟧ ⟦Mark 15:40|15:40⟧, ⟦Luke 1:80|Lk 1:80⟧ ⟦Luke 5:29|5:29⟧, ⟦John 7:30|Jo 7:30⟧, al.; seq. εἰς, ⟦Mark 2:1|Mk 2:1⟧; seq. ἐκ, (ἐξ), ⟦Matthew 1:20|Mt 1:20⟧ ⟦Matthew 21:25|21:25⟧, ⟦Mark 11:30|Mk 11:30⟧, ⟦John 3:31|Jo 3:31⟧, al.
	⟪4.⟫ Impers., ἔστι, ἦν, etc.;
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪there is⟫ (Fr. il y a), ⟪was⟫, etc.: ⟦Matthew 16:28|Mt 16:28⟧, ⟦Luke 16:19|Lk 16:19⟧, ⟦John 3:1|Jo 3:1⟧ ⟦John 5:2|5:2⟧, ⟦Romans 3:10|Ro 3:10⟧, al.; c. dat. (of the possessor; Bl., §37, 3), ⟦Matthew 16:22|Mt 16:22⟧, ⟦Luke 1:7|Lk 1:7⟧, ⟦John 18:10|Jo 18.10⟧, ⟦Romans 9:2|Ro 9:2⟧, al.; ἔστιν ὅς, ὅστις (chiefly in pl), ⟦Matthew 16:28|Mt 16:28⟧ ⟦Matthew 19:2|19:2⟧, ⟦Mark 9:1|Mk 9:1⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ c. inf., = ἔξεστιν (q.v.), ⟪it is possible⟫: ⟦Hebrews 9:5|He 9:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:20|I Co 11:20⟧, RV (but v. ICC, in l.).
⟪II.⟫ As copula uniting subject and predicate.
	⟪1.⟫ Expressing simply identity or equivalence: ⟦Matthew 5:13|Mt 5:13⟧ ⟦Matthew 14:15|14:15⟧, ⟦Luke 1:18|Lk 1:18⟧, ⟦Luke 1:19|19⟧, ⟦John 1:1|Jo 1:1⟧ ⟦John 4:19|4:19⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:9|Re 3:9⟧, al. mult.
	⟪2.⟫ Explicative, as in parable, figure, type, etc.: ⟦Matthew 13:19|Mt 13:19⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:2|I Co 9:2⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:4|10:4⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:25|11:25⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:24|Ga 4:24⟧, ⟦Revelation 17:15|Re 17:15⟧, al.; τοῦτ’ ἔστιν, ⟦Matthew 27:46|Mt 27:46⟧, ⟦Mark 7:2|Mk 7:2⟧, ⟦Romans 7:18|Ro 7:18⟧ al.; ὅ ἐστιν, ⟦Mark 3:17|Mk 3:17⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:24|Col 1:24⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:2|He 7:2⟧, al.; akin to this is the sacramental usage: ⟦Matthew 26:26|Mt 26:26-28⟧, ⟦Mark 14:22|Mk 14:22⟧, ⟦Mark 14:24|24⟧, ⟦Luke 22:19|Lk 22:19⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:24|I Co 11:24⟧ (v. ICC on Mk, I Co, ll. c.; DB, iii, 148 f.).
	⟪3.⟫ C. gen.: qual., etc., ⟦Mark 5:42|Mk 5:42⟧, ⟦Luke 3:23|Lk 3:23⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:33|I Co 14:33⟧, ⟦Hebrews 12:11|He 12:11⟧, al.; part., ⟦1 Timothy 1:20|I Ti 1:20⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:15|II Ti 1:15⟧; poss., ⟦Matthew 5:3|Mt 5:3⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:10|10⟧, ⟦Mark 12:7|Mk 12:7⟧, ⟦Luke 4:7|Lk 4:7⟧; of service or partisanship, ⟦Romans 8:9|Ro 8:9⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:12|I Co 1:12⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:7|II Co 10:7⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 2:19|II Ti 2:19⟧.
	⟪4.⟫ C. dat. (BL, §37, 3): ⟦Acts 1:8|Ac 1:8⟧ ⟦Acts 9:15|9:15⟧, ⟦Romans 4:12|Ro 4:12⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:18|I Co 1:18⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 2:14|2:14⟧, ⟦Revelation 21:7|Re 21:7⟧, al.
	⟪5.⟫ C. ptcp., as a periphrasis for the simple verb (Bl., §62, 1, 2; M, Pr., 225 ff.);
		⟪(a)⟫ c. ptcp. pf. (cl.): ⟦Matthew 10:30|Mt 10:30⟧, ⟦Luke 9:32|Lk 9:32⟧, ⟦John 3:24|Jo 3:24⟧, ⟦Acts 21:35|Ac 21:35⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:19|I Co 15:19⟧, al;
		⟪(b)⟫ c. ptcp. pr. (esp. in impf., as in Heb. and Aram.; Dalman, Words, 35 f.), ⟦Matthew 7:29|Mt 7:29⟧, ⟦Mark 1:22|Mk 1:22⟧, ⟦Luke 4:31|Lk 4:31⟧ ⟦Luke 14:1|14:1⟧, ⟦Acts 1:10|Ac 1:10⟧, al. mult., id. for imper. (M, Pr., 180f., 182f.), with ellipsis of εἰμί, ⟦Romans 12:9|Ro 12:9⟧, ⟦Romans 12:10|10⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:5|He 13:5⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ c. ptcp. aor. (cl), ⟦Luke 23:9|Lk 23:9⟧.
	⟪6.⟫ Seq. εἰς (cf. Heb. ⁨הָיָה לְ⁩), a vernac. usage (M, Pr., 71): ⟦Matthew 19:5|Mt 19:5⟧, ⟦Mark 10:8|Mk 10:8⟧, ⟦Hebrews 8:10|He 8:10⟧, al.
	⟪7.⟫ C. adv.: ⟦Matthew 19:20|Mt 19:20⟧, ⟦Mark 4:26|Mk 4:26⟧, ⟦Luke 18:11|Lk 18:11⟧, al.
	⟪8.⟫ Ellipses;
		⟪(a)⟫ of the copula (Bl., §30, 3): ⟦Matthew 8:29|Mt 8:29⟧ ⟦Matthew 24:32|24:32⟧, ⟦John 21:22|Jo 21:22⟧, ⟦John 21:23|23⟧, ⟦Hebrews 6:4|He 6:4⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ of the predicate: ἐγώ εἰμί, ⟦Matthew 14:27|Mt 14:27⟧, ⟦Mark 6:50|Mk 6:50⟧, al.; absol. (cf. ⟦Deuteronomy 32:39|De 32:39⟧; ⁨אֲנִי הוּא⁩), ⟦Mark 13:6|Mk 13:6⟧, ⟦John 4:26|Jo 4:26⟧, al. (cf. ἄπ-, ἔν-, πάρ-, συμ-πάρ-, σύν-ειμι).

